        "original_id": "10fad090-18d8-5e97-bd0f-61f5b859da4c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vladimir Nabokov, Harper Lee\n- Roles: novelist, entomologist\n- Works: To Kill a Mockingbird\n- Topics: pen names, nationalities\n\nFacts:\n- Vladimir Nabokov was born on April 22, 1899, and was also known by the pen name Vladimir Sirin.\n- Harper Lee was born on April 28, 1926, and her full name was Nelle Harper Lee.\n- Vladimir Nabokov was a Russian-American novelist and entomologist.\n- Harper Lee was an American novelist.\n- Harper Lee became widely known for the novel To Kill a Mockingbird, which was published in 1960.\n- Vladimir Nabokov died on July 2, 1977.\n- Harper Lee died on February 19, 2016.",
